# What the native build's bindings hold beside types (#593, #607). Pinning
# binds each under a key of its own, in the same layers as the types, so
# each is a struct, and a layer is a Hash of structs. Each was a mixed
# array or a list, which a native array, and a Hash of one kind of value,
# cannot hold.

# Which of the program's structs write a method of a name (#572), bound
# under `any_method_key`.
struct MethodOwners
  names
end

# How a method may be called (ADR 0093, #536), bound under
# `method_shape_key`: the fewest values it takes by place and the most,
# whether it yields, and the names it takes.
struct MethodShape
  least
  most
  yields
  labels
end

# What a combination hands its block, one type for each value, bound
# under `yields_key` (#493).
struct YieldedTypes
  types
end
